      "id": "r2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "age of Patanjali,[*] it is perfectly evident that this alleged con-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "temporaneity of Vikrama and Bhartṛihari must be at once rele-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "gated to the regions of fiction. But even if we do not accept",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "that opinion, (and let me add in passing, that for my part I do",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "not accept it, but consider it on the contrary to be quite errone-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "ous), and even if we adopt the very much more likely proposition",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "that Patanjali flourished about 144 B. C., even then, I say, it",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "is clear, that we obtain something less than nine decades for",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "all those vicissitudes in the treatment of the Mahâbhâshya and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "that line of its descent to himself which Bhartṛihari refers to",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "at length in the Vâkyapadîya.[†] And this period must, I think,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "be regarded as inadequate. Again Chandra and his colleagues",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "are said in the Râjatarangiṇî to have flourished in the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "reign of king Abhimanyu,[‡] who, according to the chronology of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "Prof. Lassen, reigned between 45 and 65. A. C.[§]; so that here",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 16,
          "text": "again we have another reason for refusing to accept the contem-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 17,
          "text": "poraneity of Bhartṛihari with the Vikrama of the Samvat Era.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "But although we have thus seen reasons for refusing to be-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "lieve that Bhartṛihari flourished about 56 B. C., it is possible, I",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "think, to make some use of the tradition of the contemporaneity",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "of Vikrama and Bhartṛihari, having regard to the conclusions of",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "footnote",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "* Professor Weber places Patanjali at 25 A. C. For the whole dis-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "cussion on the point see Indian Antiquary Vol. I., p. 300 <i>et seq.</i> Vol.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "II., p. 57 <i>et seq.</i>, p. 69 <i>et seq.</i>, p. 206 <i>et seq.</i> Goldstücker's Pâṇini <i>ad finem.</i>",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "I agree with Professors Goldstücker and Bhânḍârkar. Mr. Bhânḍârkar's",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "position does not seem to me to be shaken by Prof. Weber's letter in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "the Antiquary at p. 206, and it seems to me that the new interpretation of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "माध्यमिकान् accepted by Weber destroys the only ground for his date.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "See too “Was the Râmâyaṇa copied from Homer? p. 54.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "footnote",
